  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "The Capesize \"Blue Lhotse\" 180/2011 Daehan, Korea (SS/DD 03/2026, BWTS fitted) was committed to clients of Korea Line at USD 28,8 mill, while the \"Cape Dream\" 179/2011 Hyundai, Korea (SS/DD 06/2026, BWTS fitted) was sold a week ago at USD 28 mill. Moreover, the \"OTSL Artemis\" 177/2008 Shanghai Jiangnan, China (SS 11/2028, DD 04/2026, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) of Ocean Treasure Shipping was committed at USD 24,5 mill. For reference, the one-year-younger \"SG Express\" 180/2009 Dalian, China (SS/DD 11/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold back in October at USD 26 mill. NS United Kaiun Kaisha have committed their Post Panamax \"Century Wave\" 91/2013 Oshima, Japan (SS 07/2028, DD 06/2026, BWTS fitted) to clients of Dongguan Haichang Shipping at high USD 21 mill. Remind you that back in October, the \"Lowlands Energy\" 95/2013 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 02/2026, BWTS fitted) was committed at region USD 23 mill. On the Panamax sector, Greek owners committed the \"Stratton\" 74/2004 Hudong-Zhonghua, China (SS/DD 10/2025, BWTS fitted) to Chinese interests at low USD 7 mill. Note that a month ago, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Capricorn First\" 74/2005 Hudong-Zhonghua, China (SS/DD 06/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 8,9 mill. NGM Energy committed their Supramax \"Porthos\" 56/2010 Jiangsu, China (SS 08/2029, DD 07/2027, BWTS fitted) to undisclosed interests at USD 13,5 mill. For reference, the one-year-younger \"Diva\" 56/2011 Jiangsu, China (SS/DD 05/2026, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) was sold back in September at USD 14,75 mill. Pacific Basin Shipping committed their Handysize \"OAK Harbour\" 33/2005 Oshima, Japan (SS/DD 05/2025, BWTS fitted) at USD 8,8 mill. For comparison, the \"Sassy Sofia\" 32/2005 Kanda, Japan (SS/DD 05/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold in September at USD 9 mill. In addition, the OHBS \"Team Samba\" 31/2005 Saiki, Japan (SS/DD 03/2025, BWTS fitted) of Team Fuel Corp was committed at USD 9,4 mill.",
    "tankers": "DHT Holdings committed the VLCC \"DHT Scandinavia\" 317/2006 Hyundai Samho, Korea (SS/DD 11/2026, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) to Chinese interests at USD 43,3 mill. Note that the \"Maran Aries\" 320/2006 Daewoo, Korea (SS/DD 10/2025, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) was committed in November at USD 45,5 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "the high 6.00's fio range. A number of round trips on the same route were reported in the usd 5,000/7,000 pd range No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds continued rating primarily in the usd 6,000/8,000 pd range. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 7,000/9,000 pd range. A number of Indonesian trips into India were fixed around usd 6,000/8,000 pd. Indian trips via South America into China were reported in the usd 10,000/12,000 pd. Indian coastal trips were fixed around usd 8,000/9,000 pd. South African trips into Japan in the usd 11,000/13,000 pd plus a usd 110K/130K ballast bonus. Inter-continental trips via US Gulf in the usd 10,000/12,000 pd range. Continental trips via US Gulf into China were reported at the level of usd 17,000/19,000 pd. South American grain fronthaul in the usd 13,000/15,000 pd range plus a usd 300K/500K ballast bonus. Usd 15,000 pd plus a usd 500,000 ballast bonus for a US Gulf fronthaul. On the period front, a Kamsarmax was reported fixed in the usd 14,000 pd for 1 year employment basis delivery China. Also, a Kamsarmax was fixed on a period at the usd 12,000 pd basis delivery China for 4/6 months employment.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "Indonesian trips to China in the usd 9,000/11,000 pd range. A number of Indonesian trips into India were fixed around usd 10,000/11,000 pd. Arabian Gulf trips into India or China were reported in the usd 7,000/9,000 pd. South African trips into India in the usd 14,000/16,000 pd plus a usd 140K/160K ballast bonus. West African trips into China were fixed around usd 14,000/15,000 pd. Trips from US Gulf into Mediterranean were reported in the usd 21,000/23,000 pd. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "Japanese trips into South East Asia were fixed around usd 8,000/10,000 pd. Indian coastal trips were reported at the level of usd 8,000/9,000 pd. Continental trips into West Africa were fixed around usd 9,000/11,000 pd. West Coast Central American trips into China were reported around usd 12,000/14,000 pd. West Coast South American coastal trips were fixed around usd 15,000/16,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
